The Glasgow Jazz Festival, in its 30th iteration, will host a diverse lineup of international and local artists from June 22 to June 25. Notable international performers include Joe Locke, Alfred Pee Wee Ellis, and Kamasi Washington, alongside Scottish and UK talents such as Carol Kidd, Ryan Quigley, and Hamish Stuart. Additionally, the festival will feature young Scottish jazz musicians through the 30 Under 30 programme, highlighting emerging artists who are making significant contributions to the global jazz scene.

Jill Rodger, the director of the Glasgow Jazz Festival, expressed enthusiasm for the upcoming event. She stated, "We are thrilled to launch the 30th programme and introduce a variety of renowned artists to our stage. We are looking forward to reuniting with old friends and presenting unique collaborations. One of the highlights is the 30 Under 30 programme, which celebrates the next generation of musicians and their promising future in the jazz community."

The festival's programming underscores the importance of recognizing and nurturing emerging talent within the Scottish jazz scene. The 30 Under 30 initiative aims to provide a platform for young musicians, thereby ensuring the continuity and vibrancy of the jazz community for the next three decades.

